/target
*.o
*.ll
# Compiled Burxt outputs are bare, extensionless executables. `burxt build -o <path>`
# is the way to keep them out of the tree; without it they land in the working
# directory, where they are easy to commit by accident — two slipped into v0.0.40 that
# way, and by v0.0.70 the root held twenty-six. Ignore anything with no extension at the
# repository root, then re-admit the files that genuinely belong there: a rule that
# holds for programs nobody has written yet, rather than a list to be remembered.
/*
!/*.*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/LICENSE-APACHE
!/LICENSE-MIT
!/assets/
!/editors/
!/examples/
!/spec/
!/src/
!/tests/

# release tarballs: built by scripts/release.sh, published as GitHub release assets,
# never committed — a binary in a repository is a binary nobody can reproduce
/dist/

# editor tooling scratch
node_modules/
*.vsix

# transient delivery artifacts, and the marker Windows attaches to downloads
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*:Zone.Identifier
